OK, here's the situation. I've already ascended two barbarians, so I
thought I'd try my hand at valkyries. Well, Rose the Woman-at-arms
(Exp: 13) got into a tangle with a lich, and is now wearing a cursed
blindfold she can't remove. Thankfully, she has telepathy, but being
blinded is still a significant disadvantage. For instance, she can't
identify b/u/c status at altars. Even worse:

-- she has no identified scrolls of remove curse, and even if she did,
she couldn't read them.

-- she has no holy water, so she can't dip the blindfold into it.

-- she has some uncursed water and cursed water, but there are no
neutral altars to be found in this game, as of Dlvl 19. There are only
three altars so far, and they have all been lawful (including a lawful
temple in Minetown). So there are currently no means of producing holy
water for this neutral valkyrie.

What is my best option here? They seem to be four:

[1] Simply stumble down through further levels of the dungeon, hoping
that I come across a neutral altar.

[2] Camp out on the lawful altar levels, and hope a black unicorn comes
by, so that I can convert the lawful altar to a neutral one, and then
make some holy water.

[3] Same as [2], except use just any monster that comes by, and hope I
can convert the altar that way.

[4] Same as [2], except wait for a grey unicorn so that I can convert
myself instead of the altar. Then as a lawful valkyrie I can make holy
water at the lawful altar.

The chances for [1]-[4] seem pretty slim. Any better ideas? I have a
wand of wishing (already recharged) with two wishes left, but I really
want to avoid that option for the time being. I think it would be
interesting to solve this without wishing up some holy water.


